      "payload": {
        "jobId": "54c47ca1-73ec-4665-8bd0-c900d130c1db",
        "draftId": "artifact-output-1-linkedin_post",
        "platform": "linkedin_post",
        "text": "If your AI designs all look like boxes in boxes, it's not the model. It's the brief.\n\nMost founders tell AI: 'build me a landing page.'\n\nSo it builds the same static landing page. Same for dashboards — just box on box and leave it that way.\n\nTaste isn't a vague build request. It's a detailed description of the feel you want:\n\n'I want the chatbot to feel this way. I want the FAQs to feel this way.'\n\nWhen you give it that level of detail, it has something to work with.\n\nAnd when you need polish, don't copy — study. The public communities in Dribbble, Figma, and Spline are free for anyone to use. Not to take exactly what's there, but to see best practices for landing pages and dashboards.\n\nEdit the description of what you want first. Know it in depth.\n\nWhat feeling are you describing to AI this week — in detail?",
        "valid": true
      }
